          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e17" value="ordered set of 2..* links (closed walk)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=open;endSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c4" target="c3">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n2a" value="WELL-FORMEDNESS RULES (these catch the v1/v2 defects)&#xa;W1. One concept per variable — no compounds (“financier confidence and ROI confidence” is invalid).&#xa;W2. Direction-neutral noun phrases — no “gain”, “reduction”, “pressure increase” baked into names; direction lives in link polarity.&#xa;W3. loopType = B iff odd number of − links in the loop, else R (v2’s R7 fails this: it is balancing).&#xa;W4. Every variable must in principle be quantifiable (a unit can be stated) — required for the Vensim stage.&#xa;W5. Actual state and perceived state are different variables (environmental benefit ≠ environmental reputation).&#xa;W6. Loop IDs are stable: merging/splitting loops requires a ChangeRecord, not silent renumbering." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=#d6b656;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="160" y="430" width="440" height="250" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
