          <mxGeometry y="86" width="300" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="y1" value="SystemVariable&#xa;(CLD node)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1180" y="300" width="220" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="y2" value="Vensim SD model (stage 2)&#xa;Level / Rate / Auxiliary / Constant&#xa;from sdTypeHint + unit" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;verticalAlign=middle;dashed=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1180" y="480" width="220" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="y3" value="Excel financial model (stage 3)&#xa;line items bind to Econ attributes;&#xa;KPI rows bind to Indicators" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;verticalAlign=middle;dashed=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1180" y="600" width="220" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e9" value="is attribute of ▸ exactly 1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=open;endSize=10;exitX=0;exitY=0.25;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="b2" target="x1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e10" value="«applies»" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=open;endSize=10;dashed=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="b1" target="b2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e11" value="* records changes to 1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=open;endSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="b3" target="b2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e12" value="«must map to» 1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=open;endSize=10;dashed=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.75;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="x2" target="b2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e13" value="realizes ▸ exactly 1 (via sourceAttributeId)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=open;endSize=10;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="y1" target="b2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e18" value="«derives»" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=open;endSize=10;dashed=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="y1" target="y2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e19" value="«binds»" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=open;endSize=10;dashed=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="y2" target="y3">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n1" value="INFORMATION FLOW  FBMC → CLD (FBMC is the starting point)&#xa;1. Enumerate FBMC elements zone by zone.&#xa;2. For each element ask: which measurable attribute of it varies over time and matters to the problem? (Elements do not vary — their attributes do. “Financier” is an Actor; “financier confidence” is one of its attributes.)&#xa;3. Register the attribute: canonical name, definition, unit, dimension, sdTypeHint (via DerivationRule).&#xa;4. Decide inCldBoundary per attribute; record exclusion rationale.&#xa;5. Generate CLD variables 1:1 from in-boundary attributes — never free-typed.&#xa;6. Draw causal links only between registered variables; derive loop types.&#xa;7. Validate invariants (right) before publishing a CLD version." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=#d6b656;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="680" width="420" height="270" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n2" value="SYNCHRONIZATION INVARIANTS (check on every change)&#xa;I1. Every SystemVariable realizes exactly one MeasurableAttribute; every attribute anchors to exactly one FBMCElement → full trace: CLD variable → attribute → canvas element.&#xa;I2. Coverage: every FBMC element has ≥1 attribute in the CLD or an explicit out-of-boundary rationale.&#xa;I3. loopType is derived (B iff odd # of − links) — catches v2’s mislabelled R7.&#xa;I4. One concept per variable; direction-neutral names.&#xa;I5. Actual vs. perceived state are separate attributes (environmental benefit ≠ environmental reputation).&#xa;I6. Every Goal/Indicator maps to an attribute present in the CLD, so the model can report tri-profit (Econ, Soc, Eco).&#xa;I7. Renames/splits/merges only via ChangeRecord in the registry; FBMC and CLD are regenerated from it, never edited independently — this prevents the silent v1→v2 vocabulary drift." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=#d6b656;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="520" y="680" width="480" height="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n4" value="GENERAL PATTERN (any two domains)&#xa;Hub-and-spoke: each domain maps once to the shared registry instead of pairwise domain-to-domain mappings. Adding SD and Excel later reuses the same bridge — no new FBMC→SD or CLD→Excel mappings needed." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF9B2;strokeColor=#d6b656;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1040" y="680" width="360" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="page-generic-cld" name="4 - Generic CLD from complete FBMC">
